      "state": "present",
      "evidence": "CORE-05 (2026-11-21): the editor listens for its keys on the page (src/editor/shell/keydown.ts, dispatch.ts, keys.ts): Space plays or pauses, Home and End skip to start and end, Cmd or Ctrl with Z undoes and with Shift redoes, and the keys of one printable character the table names (J, K, L, comma, full stop, < and >, and ? for Help) are live while their switch, \"Single-key shortcuts\" in Help, is on, as the page opens, and do nothing while it is off (D183; src/editor/shell/Help.tsx, held for the visit in session.ts). Help, a button after the paragraph, opens a dialog (src/editor/kit/Dialog.tsx) listing every shortcut. The play bar after Help (src/editor/shell/PlayBar.tsx), \"Skip to start\", \"Play\" and \"Skip to end\", calls what Home, Space and End call; with nothing to play Space, K, J and L say why and start nothing, and Play is disabled and described by that reason. Journeys: character-key-shortcuts (2.1.4, both ways), fields-and-status (3.3.5, 4.1.3), reading-and-focus-order (2.4.3), pointer-cancellation (2.5.2), keyboard-task (3.2.2); keyboard functions skip-to-start-by-home, skip-to-end-by-end, open-help-by-button, open-help-by-question-mark, close-help-by-escape, single-keys-off, single-keys-on, skip-to-start-by-button, skip-to-end-by-button-space-kept, play-refused-by-space, play-refused-by-k and play-refused-by-k-, -j- and -l-on-button The timeline, a slider in the play bar (src/editor/shell/Timeline.tsx), keeps its own keys: the arrows move it, with Shift four times as far; Home, End, Page Up and Page Down on it do nothing (left to a slider, and Carbon uses none); the single keys on it say what they say elsewhere, and nothing while their switch is off."
